-upload","query_index":0,"missing_requirement_ids":[],"sources_before_filters":[{"provider_source_id":"98d872-00","url":"https://help.dropbox.com/create-upload/upload-mobile","title":"Upload files to Dropbox on a mobile device - Dropbox Help","snippet":"Dropbox\n\n# How to upload files to Dropbox on a mobile device\n\n## In this article\n\nThe information in this article applies to all Dropbox users.\n\nThe Dropbox mobile app allows you to create and upload files directly to your Dropbox account from your phone or tablet. Uploaded files sync everywhere you access your files in Dropbox.\n\nNot using Dropbox yet? See how Dropbox makes syncing files easy.\n\n## How to upload content from other mobile apps\n\nYou can upload content from other mobile apps (Photos, Messages, etc.) to your Dropbox account. To do so:\n\nNote: You must be logged into your Dropbox account on the Dropbox mobile app.\n\n## How to upload photos and videos\n\nIf you don't have camera uploads enabled, you can manually add photos to your Dropbox account. To do so: [...] Note: The Dropbox app for Windows devices does not currently support video uploads. This is due to operating system limitations.\n\n## How to upload photos overnight in iOS\n\nIf you have to upload a large amount of photos or videos from your camera app, you can use the overnight uploads feature. Overnight uploads allows you to upload your photos and videos continuously through the night, keeping the Dropbox mobile app open and dimming your device’s brightness.\n\nLearn more about overnight uploads.\n\n## How to upload audio files\n\niOS users can record audio using the Dropbox mobile app and save directly to their Dropbox account. To do so:\n\nNote: The Dropbox mobile app for Windows in S mode (Dropbox Lite) and Android devices do not currently support audio capture. [...] ## How to upload other types of files\n\nYou can also choose to create content using Microsoft Office applications.\n\nLearn more about creating content with Microsoft Office applications.\n\nIf your device has an SD card, you can upload files to Dropbox from there. To do so:\n\nNote: If you can't view your SD card when browsing for files to upload, verify that Show advanced devices is checked by tapping the menu button at the top of the screen and looking under Settings.\n\niPhone/iPad users can also upload other types of files using either of the following:\n\nYes, thanks!\n\nNot really\n\nLet us know how why it didn't help:\n\nThanks for letting us know!\n\nThanks for your feedback!\n\n### Related Articles\n\n#### Dropbox Replay FAQs\n\n#### How can I export to an SD card from my Android phone?"},{"provider_source_id":"80848b-01","url":"https://help.dropbox.com/create-upload/camera-uploads-overview","title":"How to use camera uploads - Dropbox Help","snippet":"Dropbox\n\n# How to use camera and mobile device uploads\n\n## In this article\n\nThis article describes a feature available to all Dropbox users, except:\n\n Dropbox users on Linux\n Dropbox teams who use Dropbox Enterprise Mobility Management (EMM) for Android\n\nThis article describes a feature available to all Dropbox users, except:\n\nYou can upload photos and videos from your phone or other devices to Dropbox by connecting them to your computer and using the camera uploads feature. Uploading your photos and videos to Dropbox ensures your files are securely backed up, accessible from any device, while freeing space on your phone.\n\nDropbox team admins: Learn how to turn camera uploads on or off for your team.\n\n## Turn photo and video uploads on or off on the Dropbox mobile app [...] To turn photo uploads on or off on the Dropbox mobile app for Android:\n\nTo turn photo uploads on or off on the Dropbox mobile app for iOS:\n\n## How to upload photos and videos overnight on the Dropbox mobile app\n\nNote: This feature is available on iOS devices only.\n\nIf you have to upload a large amount of photos or videos from your camera app, you can use the overnight uploads feature. Overnight uploads allows you to upload your photos and videos continuously through the night, keeping the Dropbox mobile app open and dimming your device’s brightness.  \n  \nTo turn overnight uploads on or off:\n\nNote: To successfully upload your photos and videos overnight, you must:\n\n## Turn photo and video uploads on or off in the Dropbox desktop app [...] #### Why did camera uploads use all of my cellular data?\n\nBy default, camera uploads use cellular data when WiFi isn’t available. You can change this setting by following the instructions for your device below.  \n  \nAndroid:\n\niOS:\n\n#### Can I upload iOS Live Photos?\n\nYou can upload Live Photos on the Dropbox app. Learn how to upload iOS Live photos.  \n Note: Live Photos uploaded to Dropbox from other apps will be saved as normal photos.\n\n#### What should I do if camera uploads aren't working?\n\nIf camera uploads aren't working, follow the steps in our troubleshooting guide.\n\n#### Why don’t I see the option to turn on camera uploads?\n\nIf you’re on a Dropbox team and you don’t see a camera uploads option, your admin may have turned the feature off for your team."},{"provider_source_id":"2467d3-02","url":"https://help.dropbox.com/create-upload","title":"Create and upload - Dropbox Help","snippet":"Dropbox Replay FAQs\n\nHow to manage files and projects in Dropbox Replay\n\nTurn camera uploads on/off for a Dropbox team\n\nWhy aren't my photos appearing in the Dropbox mobile app?\n\nHow to save screenshots & screen recordings\n\nHow can I export to an SD card from my Android phone?\n\n## Uploading to Dropbox DocSend\n\nFile upload limitations in Dropbox DocSend\n\nConnect cloud storage providers in Dropbox DocSend\n\nUpload and extract ZIP files in Dropbox DocSend\n\nHow to fix custom font issues in Dropbox DocSend\n\nDocuments marked as final in Dropbox DocSend\n\nHow to upload files to Dropbox DocSend\n\n## Uploading images, photos, videos, and more\n\nFix issues uploading PDFs to Dropbox Sign\n\n## Creating documents in Dropbox DocSend\n\nSignable documents in Dropbox DocSend [...] Dropbox\n\n# Create and upload\n\nLearn how to create documents, upload files and folders, and more\n\n## Creating files and folders\n\nAdd files and folders to your Dropbox account\n\nHow to copy files from Google Drive to Dropbox\n\nCreating and using folders in Dropbox\n\nPackage files and Dropbox\n\nCopy or duplicate Dropbox files\n\nWhy is Dropbox unable to upload my files?\n\nHow to Email Files to Dropbox\n\nHow to use Dropbox Paper templates\n\nHow to write content using Dropbox Dash\n\nCreate a Dropbox Paper doc\n\n## Uploading images, photos, and videos\n\nUpload files to Dropbox on a mobile device\n\nTroubleshoot issues with camera uploads\n\nHow to upload Motion & Live Photos on Dropbox\n\nSupport for HEIF (.heic) and HEVC photo and video files\n\nDropbox Replay FAQs [...] How to pre-fill data in Dropbox Forms\n\nAdd merge fields to a template in Dropbox Sign\n\nHow to use Dropbox Sign\n\nDuplicate a template or template link in Dropbox Sign\n\nCreate and save signatures in Dropbox Sign\n\nAdd Dropbox Sign signature on smartphones\n\nHow to create Dropbox Sign templates\n\nHow to use the Dropbox Sign template gallery\n\nHow to use AI Auto-place Fields in Dropbox Sign\n\n## Scanning documents\n\nScan documents using the Dropbox mobile app\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n## Other ways to get help\n\nContact support icon\n\n### Contact support\n\nLearn about your support options, file a support ticket, and check the status of open tickets.\n\nCommunity forum icon\n\n### Community\n\nConnect with other Dropbox customers to get answers and learn best practices.\n\nLearn icon\n\n### Learn"},{"provider_source_id":"8608bf-03","url":"https://help.dropbox.com/create-upload/add-files","title":"Uploading to Dropbox: how to add files and folders to your Dropbox account - Dropbox Help","snippet":"Dropbox\n\n# Uploading to Dropbox: how to add files and folders to your Dropbox account\n\n## In this article\n\nThe information in this article applies to all Dropbox users.\n\nYou can upload files and folders to your Dropbox account on dropbox.com and the Dropbox desktop app. Each file or folder uploaded on dropbox.com can be up to 350 GB. Each file or folder uploaded on the Dropbox desktop app can be up to 2 TB.\n\nYou can also upload files with the Dropbox mobile app.\n\nTip: To upload files larger than 350 GB, we recommend downloading the Dropbox desktop app on your computer and uploading your file from there. You can also compress your file to reduce its size to under 350 GB, and then upload it via dropbox.com. Learn more about Dropbox file size limits. [...] ## Upload files and folders to your Dropbox account\n\nNote: The option to import from Microsoft OneDrive may only be available on certain individual Dropbox plans.\n\n### On the Dropbox desktop app\n\nNotes:\n\n You can save new or existing files directly into the Dropbox folder.\n Files in the Dropbox folder on your computer automatically sync everywhere you access your files in Dropbox, including dropbox.com and the mobile app.\n\nNotes:\n\nWatch this video for a quick overview of how to upload and download files in Dropbox.\n\nYes, thanks!\n\nNot really\n\nLet us know how why it didn't help:\n\nThanks for letting us know!\n\nThanks for your feedback!\n\n### Related Articles\n\n#### Copy or duplicate Dropbox files\n\n#### How to use Dropbox Paper templates\n\n#### Create a Dropbox Paper doc"},{"provider_source_id":"e4b080-04","url":"https://help.dropbox.com/create-upload/upload-live-photos","title":"How to upload Motion & Live Photos on Dropbox - Dropbox Help","snippet":"### How to share Motion Photos\n\nTo share your Motion Photos with others, you can create and share a link, invite them to a file folder, or send directly through your preferred sharing method.\n\n## How to upload Live Photos on iOS\n\nYou can upload and share Live Photos via the Dropbox mobile app.\n\nNote:To access this feature, make sure your Dropbox mobile app is updated to the latest version.\n\nTo upload your Live Photos:\n\nNote: To preview a Live Photo, tap the play button on the Live Photo or press and hold the Live Photo.\n\n### How to share Live Photos\n\nTo share your Live Photos with others, you can create and share a link, invite them to a file folder, or send directly through your preferred sharing method.\n\nYes, thanks!\n\nNot really\n\nLet us know how why it didn't help: [...] Dropbox\n\n# How to upload Motion Photos and Live Photos to Dropbox\n\n## In this article\n\nThe information in this article applies to all Dropbox users.\n\nNote: You can also view and share Motion Photos and Live Photos on dropbox.com. This option is currently only available on computers using the Google Chrome browser.\n\n## How to upload Motion Photos on Android\n\nYou can upload and share Motion Photos via the Dropbox mobile app.\n\nNote: To access this feature, make sure your Dropbox mobile app is updated to the latest version.\n\nTo upload your Motion Photos:\n\nNote: You can also upload Motion Photos to Dropbox using your camera app.\n\n### How to share Motion Photos"}],"source_ids_after_filters":["98d872-00","80848b-01","8608bf-03","e4b080-04"]},{"stage":"official_read","url":"https://help.dropbox.com/create-upload/upload-mobile","status":"read","sha256":"5e686ea99b09dc875b95347105aad601c681dee4ee3898379bdb5f77e21feb8e","byte_count":697818,"final_url":"https://help.dropbox.com/create-upload/upload-mobile","latency_ms":4341},{"stage":"official_read","url":"https://help.dropbox.com/create-upload/camera-uploads-overview","status":"read","sha256":"ffba05016a8c1c66ef4f148129b78565a7912fbfbc0dcf20a08ff13af07c0d9e","byte_count":761000,"final_url":"https://help.dropbox.com/create-upload/camera-uploads-overview","latency_ms":4298},{"stage":"llm","attempt":1,"retry_hint":null,"response_metadata":{"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":6891,"output_tokens":273